  "title": "Tusk defends overhaul of Poland’s judiciary",
  "summary": "Prime minister Donald Tusk vowed to see through a contested overhaul of the country’s constitutional court, declaring that ‘in certain matters, there can be no compromise’ despite opposition accusations of staging an institutional coup.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "Tusk defended the constitutional court’s overhaul, asserting it is essential to restore a tribunal crippled by years of political disputes.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Opposition claims Tusk staged an institutional coup, but he defended his stance, citing the need for progress despite protests.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The court’s rebuilding was highlighted in a televised address on Saturday.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
