      "title": "Tusk defends overhaul of Poland’s constitutional court despite protests",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/31/donald-tusk-defends-overhaul-poland-constitutional-court-despite-protests",
      "description": "<p>Prime minister says shake-up is vital to restore tribunal crippled by years of political disputes</p><p>Poland’s prime minister, Donald Tusk, has vowed to see through a contested overhaul of the country’s constitutional court, declaring that “in certain matters, there can be no compromise”.</p><p>In <a href=\"https://x.com/donaldtusk/status/2116606129811722534\">a prime-time television address on Saturday night</a>, Tusk was defiant, despite overnight protests that saw riot police drafted to protect the court’s building, saying the shake-up was vital to restore a tribunal crippled by years of political disputes.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/31/donald-tusk-defends-overhaul-poland-constitutional-court-despite-protests\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
